# SPP manual bidding — bid date **2026-08-15**

**Read this caveat first.** The run fired at **08:00 CT**, not the 13:00 cron slot. Under the ≥10am rule that makes `bid_dt = 2026-08-15` and `dt = 2026-08-14` — **today**. So the "DA candidates" set is **today's cleared DA, not the bid date's**. Tomorrow's DA has not cleared yet. Every DA figure below is today's DA used as a proxy for tomorrow. That weakens the rung-5 "DA is likely wrong" calls specifically (I'm inferring tomorrow's DA from today's), but it *strengthens* the RT evidence: today's DA is fully cleared and today's RT hours 1–8 are in, so today gives a clean same-day DA-vs-RT read.

**Attribution PDF window: 2026-08-01 to 2026-08-07** — a week stale, analysis dates 08-01 to 08-07. It covers 19 of 48 candidates; **29 candidates have no write-up at all**. For those, the calls rest on RT evidence and the zonal setup only. Several PDF write-ups name outages that have since expired — flagged individually below.

**Tomorrow's zonal setup** (median percentile, on/off-peak wind / on/off-peak load):

| Zone | ow | fw | ol | fl | Flag |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 6 | **0** | 35 | 72 | **Wind at the 0–16th pct all day — the most extreme reading on the board** |
| 2 | 41 | 58 | 46 | 58 | neutral |
| 3 | 71 | **85** | 64 | 75 | **Wind 84–97th pct HE3–HE10, collapsing to 6–13th pct after HE21**; load 77–81st pct HE16–19 |
| 4 | 74 | 75 | 67 | 62 | Wind 74–87th pct overnight–HE11; **load 80.6th pct HE17–18** |
