## GO LONG

**Rung 1 — outage in effect on the bid date**

1. **ln6_me4-sw51** — Mustang OKGE–SW 5th 138 kV out **08-03 → 08-27 14:00**, confirmed in the bid-date schedule and in `linked_outages`. RT 10/30 days and climbing: -7,028 → -8,658 → -3,545 → -6,039 → **-10,308** yesterday. PDF (08-05): *"extreme peak load conditions in the OKGE zone… OKGE load exceeded its day-ahead forecast by 325 MW during the peak hour."* Today's DA concentrates HE14–20; zone 4 load hits 80.6 at HE17–18. Conditions reproduce. **Load, zone 4** (lift 16.2 vs wind −1.0). *Zone is the fallback — the sheet has no mapping — but the PDF names OKGE, which is zone 4 here, so it happens to agree.* **High conviction.**

2. **lnosage_og-webbtap4** — Morrison–Sooner 138 kV out **through 09-17 15:30**, which the PDF says raises binding odds **7.17x**. RT 17/30, -5,204 yesterday, -572 already by HE8 today. PDF (08-03): *"peak wind generation in the OKGE zone pushing power toward the CSWS zone."* Lift is a clean wind story — **wind 1.54, load −0.01, zone 3** (sheet-mapped). Zone 3 wind is 84–97th pct HE3–HE10 and zone 4 wind 74–87th pct overnight. Today's DA is concentrated HE1–8 and HE21–24. **Long the overnight and morning hours.** **High conviction.**

3. **lnfirstcrk-roanrdge** — **two 345 kV outages in effect on the bid date**: St Joe–Fairport (through 08-21, 2.77x risk) and Cooper–Fairport (through 10-16, 1.99x). PDF (08-03): *"the outage removed a parallel path, increasing the flow on the monitored element."* RT printed -4,690 on 08-08 and -1,569 yesterday, against a today-DA of **-51**. **Load, zone 4** (lift 6.63 vs wind 1.98, sheet-mapped); zone 4 load peaks 80.6 at HE17–18. Good disagreement. **Medium-high.**

**Rung 3 — binding in RT, DA not pricing it (the highest-value disagreements)**

4. **xfmrbrook_ln-brook_ln** — **RT 24 of the last 30 days, and DA has been exactly 0 on every one of the last 11.** Escalating: -1,254 → **-5,684** yesterday. PDF (08-04): *"peak load conditions in the SPRM and EES zones… structurally loaded by regional wind flowing toward these load centers… the day-ahead market cleared without binding."* EROGERS Avoca–East Rogers 161 kV (10.5% LODF, 2.09x) is **active through 08-31**. **Load** (lift 3.86 vs wind −0.34). *Zone-4 fallback is the wrong zone — SPRM is zone 3 — so the lift magnitude is low-confidence, but the direction matches the PDF, and zone 3 load is 77–81st pct HE16–19.* **High conviction on the disagreement, medium on the zone.**

5. **lnaur1241-rdspg5** — **RT 11/30, -4,839 yesterday, and DA has been 0 every single day for 11 days.** PDF (08-01) describes exactly this: *"bound heavily in real-time (-1002 m-value) while clearing unconstrained in the day-ahead market… driven by a massive 1,602 MW wind over-forecast in real-time, coupled with a 100 MW under-forecast in local EDE load. Wind is a strong historical load driver (3.06x multiplier), while EDE load provides relief."* Lift confirms: **wind 1.67, load −0.28**. Tomorrow is high wind + soft local load in the EDE geography (zone 3 wind 85–97th pct HE3–HE10, zone 3 on-peak load only 48–55 midday). Avoca–East Rogers (2.13x) active through 08-31. **The best single setup on the board. High conviction.**

6. **xfmrnowst1-nowst1** — **RT 20/30 and escalating monotonically**: -2,792 → -11,066 → -9,185 → -9,317 → -15,175 → **-26,978 yesterday, the largest RT print of the week.** Today's DA collapsed to **-226** after running -6,500 to -9,000 all week — a very large disagreement if it carries into tomorrow. PDF (08-05): *"extreme peak load in the OKGE zone… actual OKGE load exceeded the Day-Ahead forecast by 237 MW during the peak afternoon hours."* **Load, zone 4** (lift 9.56 vs wind 1.21, sheet-mapped), and zone 4 load peaks 80.6 at HE17–18. Morrison–Sooner still active through 09-17. **High conviction.**

7. **lnfulton_c-pat_wx** — RT 11/30, escalating to **-1,724** yesterday, **DA 0 on all 11 days.** No PDF write-up, no precedent in the Aug 8–22 window of either 2024 or 2025, and the lift ran on the zone-4 fallback (load 6.67, wind 1.87 — **low confidence, wrong zone likely**). Pure disagreement play. **Speculative, small.**

**Rung 2/4 — conditions reproduce, momentum**

8. **lnmonett-aur1241** — RT 20/30, -3,832 yesterday, and **-876 in today's hours 1–8, the largest early-hour RT print on the board.** PDF (08-03): *"driven primarily by peak regional wind generation and peak local load in the EDE zone."* Its acute trigger, Stockton–Morgan 161 kV, **expired 08-06**, but Avoca–East Rogers (1.47x) is active through 08-31, and the wind driver reproduces strongly overnight. Lift **doesn't separate** — wind 1.96 vs load 1.98 — and it was measured on zone 4 while the constraint is physically EDE ≈ zone 3. **Long the overnight/morning window** where zone 3 wind is 85–97th pct. **Medium-high.**

9. **lnclevlnd7-clev_aec** — bound in RT **7 days straight** (-324, -468, -857, -648, -768, -1,009, and -158 by HE8 today), 12/30 days. Not in the PDF. **Strongest seasonal precedent on the board: 5 RT days in Aug 8–22 2024, and 9 days / -29,031 in Aug 8–22 2025** — this exact calendar window, two years running. Lift **doesn't separate** — wind 0.75, load 0.36, zone 4 sheet-mapped. Steady daily binder, not a spike. **Medium, size moderate.**

10. **xfmrcimarron-cimarron** — RT 14/30, steady -500 to -1,100 daily, -185 by HE8 today; DA rising to -3,376. PDF (08-07): *"a chronic structural bottleneck in central Oklahoma that facilitates the flow of wind energy from western Oklahoma to load centers in the east,"* driven by peak OKGE load **and** high OKGE wind. Seasonal precedent: 7 RT days / -17,386 in Aug 8–22 2024. Lift is **weak and doesn't separate** — load 1.41, wind 0.31 — and the sheet says zone 2 while the PDF says OKGE (zone 4); **note the disagreement, prefer the PDF's zone.** The call rests on RT persistence + precedent, not on the lift. **Medium.**

11. **lnvinetap3-nhays** — RT 10/30 including -7,983 on 08-11; **today RT is already -179 against a full-day DA of only -113** — RT has overtaken the whole day's DA by HE8. Seasonal: 6 RT days / -13,204 in Aug 8–22 2025. PDF (08-03): *"high wind generation in the WR MIDW and OKGE zones."* But the measured lift **contradicts the PDF** — load 1.78 vs wind 1.15 on zone 2 (sheet-mapped) — and zone 2 is neutral tomorrow on both. **Medium-low; momentum and precedent carry it, conditions are neutral.**

12. **lncrescent-ctnwd1** — RT 6/30 but perfectly steady (-134 to -486 daily) with DA tracking it closely, so no big disagreement — just a reliable small binder. **Cleanest wind signal in the whole run: lift 4.52 on wind, −0.44 on load.** Zone 4 wind is 74–87th pct overnight. Not in the PDF; zone-4 fallback, so the zone is unverified. **Small long, overnight hours.**

13. **lntulsa_no-46_st_tp** — rare (0.04% baseline) but printed **-1,304 in RT yesterday against a DA of -1**. PDF (08-06): *"driven by peak summer load in the CSWS zone… no transmission outages were identified as contributing factors."* That last clause is worth doubting: **Igloo Valley–Tulsa North 345 kV is out through 09-02**, plus GATUSI–ONETA and GATUSI–NE_COAL 345 kV through 2027 and Collinsville–Owasso 69 kV through 09-19 — substantial Tulsa-area topology the PDF's model didn't attach. Zone 4 load 80.6 at HE17–18 reproduces the driver. **Speculative, small.**

