## GO SHORT

**Rung 1 — the trigger expired, or relief is back on**

1. **lnweav-tallgras** — the cleanest short on the board. **DA has priced it every day for 11 days (-5,724 and -5,942 on 08-12/08-13, -511 today) and RT has been exactly zero on all 11 — 0 RT days in the last 30.** The PDF (08-07) gives the mechanism precisely: the RT premium that day came from the **cancellation** of the BUTL–OTTERCRK 138 kV outage, *"a scheduled outage that provided significant relief (39.4% LODF) in the DA model but was absent in RT."* **That relief outage is back on and scheduled through 08-21 16:00.** Meanwhile the aggravating CANA–Fowler outage (6.18x) **expired 08-07 13:00**. Relief on, aggravation off, RT dead for a month. **Load, zone 4** (lift 3.18). **High conviction.**

2. **xfmrpotter_s-potter_s** — binds in RT **every single day (31/30)** but tiny (-67 to -562), so the DA at -203/-643 is the overpriced side. PDF (08-03): the acute trigger was *"SPS zonal load surged to peak levels (avg 5,517 MW),"* predisposed by the DeGrasse–Knob Hill 138 kV outage — which **expired 08-05**. **Tomorrow SPS load is at the 0–10th percentile all day, the most extreme collapse on the board — the named driver is directly contradicted.** The lift (load 3.66) ran on the **zone-4 fallback, which is the wrong zone**; on the correct zone 5 the setup is decisively against. **Medium-high, with the caveat that it binds daily regardless of conditions.** Watch CROSSRDS–HOBBS 345 kV (new, 08-12 → 09-08) as the offsetting risk.

3. **lnrussett-sbrown** — looks like a monster at RT 28/30, but the trend has **collapsed**: -4,030 (08-06) → -2,766 → -92 → -380 → -1,899 → -840 → -46 → **-102 yesterday**, -272 today. **DA has not moved — a flat -1,743 to -2,914 every single day.** PDF (08-06): the driver was *"the outage of the parallel Pittsburg–Valliant 345kV line… 30.5% flow impact"* — that outage **expired 08-07 17:00**, and the secondary CRIVRAEP XF1 **expires today at 16:00**. Neither is in the bid-date schedule. **Wind, zone 3** (lift 1.07 vs load −0.43, sheet-mapped) — and zone 3 wind *is* high overnight, which is the one thing arguing against this short. **Concentrate the short on on-peak and evening hours, where zone 3 wind falls to the 6–13th percentile.** **Medium-high.**

4. **xfmrduncan-duncan** — DA still -3,605 today, but PDF (08-07) names the acute trigger as *"the transmission outage of the Walters 2 – Walters 2 69kV line… 32.26% LODF"* — that outage **ended 08-13 16:00**, and RT immediately decayed from -7,739 (08-12) to -2,984 (08-13) to zero in today's hours 1–8. The only surviving outage (El Reno Junction–Red Corn Tap, through 09-25) carries a **0.00x risk multiplier**. Residual driver is CSWS load: **lift 1.91 load / 0.53 wind, zone 2 sheet-mapped — and zone 2 load is mid at 46/58, not peak.** Conditions do not reproduce. **Medium-high.**

**Rung 5 — DA pricing it while conditions say otherwise**

5. **lnommarlo4-rsh_sprg_rev23** — DA -3,546 yesterday and -2,869 today, concentrated HE14–20; **RT zero on all 11 days, 0 RT days in 30.** The PDF (08-07) is unusually explicit about the mechanism: *"Historical analysis confirms this constraint is exclusively driven by peak load conditions. The day-ahead model over-forecasted WFEC zonal load by 231 MW during the peak afternoon hours, causing the constraint to bind at -$482/MWh in DA. In real-time, the lower actual load kept flows below the thermal limit, resulting in a $0/MWh RT shadow price."* No outages, then or on the bid date. Lift is load 18.63 on the zone-4 fallback; **the physical zone is WFEC ≈ zone 2, where load is mid at 46/58 — nowhere near the peak the write-up requires.** Same mechanism, same non-peak load. **High conviction.**

6. **lnharbingr-walkmy1** — DA jumped to **-2,193 today** from -222 and -698 earlier in the week, while **RT is zero on all 11 days and 0/30.** Not in the PDF. Lift is pure load (10.47 vs wind −1.00) but on the **zone-4 fallback — low confidence, and no PDF zone to prefer instead.** Today's DA is off-peak-weighted (HE16–24 and HE1–7) where zone 4 load is only 51–67th pct. **Medium.**

7. **lnarcad7-jones_ka** — appeared in DA today at **-1,110 with zero DA on the previous 10 days and zero RT on all 11; 0/30 RT days**, baseline binding rate 0.30%. No PDF write-up. A one-day DA appearance on a rare constraint with no RT history and no attribution is the standard DA artefact. **Load, zone 4 fallback — low confidence on the attribution, but the short doesn't depend on it.** **Medium, small size.**

8. **lnstilwell-redel5** — RT 16/30 but **decaying to nothing**: -914 (08-10) → 0 → -27 → -32 → 0 today, while DA re-priced up to -1,288. PDF (08-04): peak MPS load, *"exacerbated by a scheduled relief outage that was not taken in real-time."* The two relief outages are now **active on the bid date** — Pleasant Hill MPS–Raymore (8.2% LODF, **0.14x** risk) through 09-04 and 13 & 40–Warrensburg Plant through 10-30 — while the aggravating SHEF and SEDPLT outages **expired 08-12**. Lift load 2.36 / wind 0.92, zone 4 sheet-mapped. Caveat: 9 RT days in the Aug 8–22 2025 window, though for only -898 total. **Medium-low, small.**

9. **pssooner-sooner** — DA leapt to **-1,240 today** from -33 and -244; **RT zero on all 11 days, 0/30.** Not in the PDF. Lift **does not separate at all** — wind 1.10 vs load 1.06, zone-4 fallback. Counter-argument to flag: **Morrison–Sooner 138 kV is genuinely out through 09-17**, which could be what the DA is repricing — but that outage has been in place since 07-23 and RT has never printed. **Low-medium, small.**

**Do not go long — but there is nothing to sell**

- **lnraun-tekamho** has real momentum (RT 8/30, -3,307 yesterday, -427 by HE8 today) and DA at 0 all week, which normally makes it a rung-3 long. **It fails rung 2 decisively.** PDF (08-07): *"heavily loaded by wind generation in the northern SPP/MISO footprint (WAUE, NSP, ALTW) transferring power south to OPPD."* Lift confirms wind-driven (1.07 wind, 0.00 load, **zone 1, sheet-mapped**). **Zone 1 wind tomorrow is at the 0–16th percentile every hour of the day.** The driver is absent. Since DA is already 0, there is no premium to sell — **stand aside, do not long it on the RT print.**

